\subsection{GDALExtendedDataTypeR class}{

Objects of class \code{GDALExtendedDataTypeR} are obtained from
\code{arr$getDataType()} or \code{att$getDataType()}. Instances can also be
created using the factory functions \code{edtCreate()}, \code{edtCreateString()},
and \code{edtCreateCompound()}. An extended data type describes the type of
individual elements in an array or attribute, and may be numeric, string,
or compound.

\verb{$getName()}\cr
Returns the type name (e.g., \code{"Float64"}, \code{"String"}).

\verb{$getClass()}\cr
Returns the type class as an integer: \code{0} for \code{NUMERIC}, \code{1} for
\code{STRING}, \code{2} for \code{COMPOUND}.

\verb{$getClassAsString()}\cr
Returns the type class as a character string.

\verb{$getNumericDataType()}\cr
For numeric types, returns the \code{GDALDataType} integer code.

\verb{$getNumericDataTypeAsString()}\cr
For numeric types, returns the data type name (e.g., \code{"Float64"},
\code{"Int16"}).

\verb{$getSize()}\cr
Returns the element size in bytes.

\verb{$getMaxStringLength()}\cr
For string types, returns the maximum string length (0 = unlimited).

\verb{$getComponents()}\cr
For compound types, returns a list of component descriptions.

\verb{$canConvertTo(other)}\cr
Returns \code{TRUE} if this type can be converted to \code{other} (a
\code{GDALExtendedDataTypeR} object).

\verb{$equals(other)}\cr
Returns \code{TRUE} if this type is equal to \code{other}.
}

