\note{
Requires GDAL >= 3.1.0 for multidimensional raster support. Some
methods require later GDAL versions (e.g., \verb{$getResampled()} requires
GDAL >= 3.4). Methods that are optionally supported by drivers (e.g.,
\verb{$createGroup()}, \verb{$resize()}, \verb{$rename()}) may return \code{FALSE} or raise
an error if the driver does not support the operation.

The main drivers supporting the multidimensional API are \code{netCDF},
\code{HDF5}, \code{Zarr}, \code{MEM}, \code{TileDB}, and \code{VRT}. Use
\code{getMultiDimDrivers()} to list available drivers on the current system.

The \verb{$read()} method returns data with dimensions reversed relative to
GDAL's C ordering, to match R's column-major array convention. The
first GDAL dimension (slowest varying) becomes the last R dimension.

The following GDAL Multidim API features are not yet exposed and may be
added in future versions:
\code{GDALMDArray::GetCoordinateVariables()} (retrieve coordinate variables),
\code{GDALMDArray::IsRegularlySpaced()} (test for regular spacing),
\code{GDALMDArray::GuessGeoTransform()} (infer geotransform from dimensions),
\code{GDALMDArray::GetStatistics()} (read cached statistics),
\code{GDALMDArray::GetGridded()} (on-the-fly gridding, GDAL >= 3.4),
\code{GDALMDArray::GetMeshGrid()} (static, GDAL >= 3.12),
\code{GDALGroup::CopyFrom()},
\code{GDALGroup::SubsetDimensionFromSelection()} (GDAL >= 3.4).
}
